## Item 2 — ZoneWorld runner self-invocation (D, deterministic when invoked by a relative path)
- `framework/languages/java/samples/java/ZoneWorld/run_sample.sh:10` does `cd "$ROOT_DIR"`, then `:34`
  (and any other `bash "$0"` site) re-invokes itself for the isolation children (`--b8-child`, G4).
  When the script was started as `bash framework/languages/java/samples/java/ZoneWorld/run_sample.sh`
  from the repo root, `$0` is relative and no longer resolves after the `cd`:
  `bash: framework/languages/java/samples/java/ZoneWorld/run_sample.sh: No such file or directory`
  → ZW-B8 fails, `zoneworld=completed` withheld. Fix: resolve the script's absolute path once at the
  top (before the cd) and use it for every self-invocation; check the Kotlin ZoneWorld runner and
  `run_sample.ps1` for the same pattern and align. Verify: `bash framework/languages/java/samples/java/ZoneWorld/run_sample.sh`
  from the repo root 1× green (`zoneworld=completed`), and `(cd .../ZoneWorld && bash ./run_sample.sh)` 1× green.

